- SOCKS Fastjson source audit: extended `RuntimeConfigFixtures` to invoke Fastjson 2.0.63 for every BMP unit before a route and `null`, C0 units 0–32 at six token boundaries, and every Java whitespace/control candidate at those boundaries. Direct observations capture U+001A handling at two root boundaries. Java accepts the existing leading whitespace/control set plus BOM/U+FFFE; inside a root object it additionally accepts U+0080, U+0088–U+008A, U+008C–U+008D, and NBSP. The refreshed 492-constructor fixture SHA-256 is `a43fd38b2cb6c04f515af9d8bd88b2141d4300547b7a2a439f06c0ae4902c3fb`.
